  "sourceUse": "The adopted 2026–2027 OER B4.2 confirms 180 EC. The study guide elective record itself has zero credits because it is a placeholder, while its group and the OER set 18 EC. The OER gives semester 2 for the 24 EC internship and thesis and governs the illustrated route. The guide shows a broader offering window for registration; the public overview puts the placement in blocks 5–6. The guide dates Medical Images and Signals to block 4 and the OER confirms semester 2, rather than relying on the overview’s block label.",
  "progression": {
    "yearOne": "Six prescribed units total 60 EC. The public degree description identifies introductory HTML and Python in the first course and a Java foundation in Developing Healthcare Applications. Medical contexts and logic are taught alongside computing.",
    "yearTwo": "Articles B4.5 and B7.3 require the ordinary student to meet the 48 EC first-year binding study advice standard for second-year education and assessment. The 60 EC second year covers clinical epidemiology, information exchange, entrepreneurship, learning healthcare, software engineering and strategic information management.",
    "yearThree": "B4.5 requires all 60 EC of year one and at least 48 EC of year two before third-year education and assessment. B4.2 locates summative academic and professional competency portfolio assessment during Strategic Information Management. Under B4.5(3), passing that competency line is also required before the 24 EC internship and thesis. The Bèta-gamma exception belongs to a different route.",
    "openChoice": "B4.3 preserves 18 EC in the first semester of year three. Non-preapproved choices need prior permission, with a reasoned submission before 1 May of the preceding academic year. Substantial overlap with compulsory or other elective units is excluded. Choices already listed as approved need no further Examination Board permission."
  }
